    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrīcē</span></b> ,
		ēs, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrīca</span></b> , ae,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρίκη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the tamarisk, a kind
				of shrub</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 13, 21, 37, § 116</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">24, 9, 41, §
				67</span></i>.—Prov., to signify something impossible: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pinguia corticibus sudent electra myricae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 8, 54</span></i>
			.</div>
